version: 4
data:
  attachedData:
    trivet:
      testSuites: []
      version: 1
  graphs:
    main_challenge_v2:
      metadata:
        description: >-
          Grounded monthly-letter workflow. A deterministic Python engine writes
          build/facts.json (audited numbers, benchmarks, recommendations, macro).
          This graph NARRATES those facts in Portuguese with Anthropic Claude and
          never invents a number. Fixes the v1 issues: hardcoded Windows paths,
          hallucinated macro, wrong client name, no profitability, no recommendations.
        id: main_challenge_v2
        name: main_challenge
      nodes:
        '[factsPath]:text "Facts Path"':
          data:
            text: build/facts.json
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Read Facts" factsRead/path
          visualData: 10/200/330/1//
        '[factsRead]:readFile "Read Facts"':
          data:
            asBinary: false
            errorOnMissingFile: true
            path: ''
            usePathInput: true
          outgoingConnections:
            - content->"Prompt Performance" pPerf/facts
            - content->"Prompt Macro" pMacro/facts
            - content->"Prompt Recommendations" pRecs/facts
            - content->"Prompt Letter" pLetter/facts
          visualData: 380/200/280/2//
        '[macroPath]:text "Macro Path"':
          data:
            text: Input/XP - Macro analysis.txt
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Read Macro" macroRead/path
          visualData: 10/680/330/3//
        '[macroRead]:readFile "Read Macro"':
          data:
            asBinary: false
            errorOnMissingFile: true
            path: ''
            usePathInput: true
          outgoingConnections:
            - content->"Prompt Macro" pMacro/macro_report
          visualData: 380/680/280/4//
        '[pPerf]:prompt "Prompt Performance"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
            promptText: |-
              ## Task: Summarize portfolio performance (grounded)

              You receive a FACTS JSON computed by an audited engine. Summarize the
              client's performance for the reference month. Use ONLY numbers present
              in FACTS. NEVER invent or alter a figure.

              Rules:
              - The equities sleeve return is MEASURED; the funds and total return are
                an ESTIMATE (CDI proxy, monthly fund NAV not provided) — say so plainly.
              - Mention the best/worst stock of the month and the comparison vs CDI/IPCA.
              - 4-6 sentences, professional, plain language. Output language: English
                (this is an intermediate summary; the final letter is Portuguese).

              ### FACTS
              {{facts}}
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Chat Performance" cPerf/prompt
          visualData: 720/60/300/5//
        '[cPerf]:chat "Chat Performance"':
          data:
            model: claude-sonnet-4-6
            temperature: 0.2
            top_p: 1
            useTopP: false
            maxTokens: 1024
            enableFunctionUse: false
            cache: false
            useAsGraphPartialOutput: true
          outgoingConnections:
            - response->"Prompt Letter" pLetter/performance
          visualData: 1060/60/240/6//
        '[pMacro]:prompt "Prompt Macro"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
            promptText: |-
              ## Task: Summarize the macro outlook (source-restricted)

              Summarize the macro backdrop for an investor letter. You MUST use only
              figures that appear in FACTS.macro (transcribed from XP's 06/02/2025
              report) and/or the raw macro text. Do NOT introduce any number that is
              not in these sources (this fixes the v1 hallucination where Selic/FX
              were invented).

              Anchor figures to repeat verbatim from FACTS.macro: Selic terminal,
              IPCA 2025, FX end-2025, GDP 2025. 3-4 sentences, English (intermediate).

              ### FACTS
              {{facts}}

              ### Raw macro report (reference only)
              {{macro_report}}
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Chat Macro" cMacro/prompt
          visualData: 720/380/300/7//
        '[cMacro]:chat "Chat Macro"':
          data:
            model: claude-sonnet-4-6
            temperature: 0.2
            top_p: 1
            useTopP: false
            maxTokens: 1024
            enableFunctionUse: false
            cache: false
            useAsGraphPartialOutput: true
          outgoingConnections:
            - response->"Prompt Letter" pLetter/macro_outlook
          visualData: 1060/380/240/8//
        '[pRecs]:prompt "Prompt Recommendations"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
            promptText: |-
              ## Task: Present the recommendations (grounded)

              FACTS.recommendations holds an explainable, rule-based set of actions
              (deploy idle cash, rebalance vs target, trim concentration, review the
              impaired non-dividend stock, etc.), each with a rationale and amount.

              Turn the top recommendations into a concise advisory paragraph. Keep the
              amounts and tickers exactly as in FACTS. Connect them to the moderate
              risk profile and to the high-Selic macro context. 4 sentences, English.

              ### FACTS
              {{facts}}
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Chat Recommendations" cRecs/prompt
          visualData: 720/700/300/9//
        '[cRecs]:chat "Chat Recommendations"':
          data:
            model: claude-sonnet-4-6
            temperature: 0.2
            top_p: 1
            useTopP: false
            maxTokens: 1024
            enableFunctionUse: false
            cache: false
            useAsGraphPartialOutput: true
          outgoingConnections:
            - response->"Prompt Letter" pLetter/recommendations
          visualData: 1060/700/240/10//
        '[pLetter]:prompt "Prompt Letter"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
            promptText: |-
              ## Task: Write the monthly investment letter (PORTUGUESE)

              Integrate the three summaries into a single, polished letter in
              Brazilian Portuguese, ready to send to the client.

              Hard rules:
              - Address the client by FACTS.client.first_name (e.g., "Prezado Albert,").
                NEVER use a placeholder name like "João".
              - Sign off with FACTS.advisor.name and code.
              - Use ONLY numbers already present in the summaries / FACTS. Do not invent.
              - Keep the funds/total return framed as an estimate where FACTS says so.
              - Up to two pages (~500 words), paragraphs (no bullets), warm but precise,
                in the voice of an elite XP advisor: clear, proactive, trustworthy.
              - Add one short footnote sentence: equity prices reflect the statement of
                FACTS.meta.snapshot_date while market benchmarks use the reference-month
                close, so windows may differ slightly.

              ### Client risk profile
              {{facts}}

              ### 1. Performance summary
              {{performance}}

              ### 2. Macro outlook summary
              {{macro_outlook}}

              ### 3. Recommendations summary
              {{recommendations}}
          outgoingConnections:
            - output->"Chat Letter" cLetter/prompt
          visualData: 1360/340/320/11//
        '[cLetter]:chat "Chat Letter"':
          data:
            model: claude-sonnet-4-6
            temperature: 0.3
            top_p: 1
            useTopP: false
            maxTokens: 1500
            enableFunctionUse: false
            cache: false
            useAsGraphPartialOutput: true
          outgoingConnections: []
          visualData: 1740/340/260/12//
  metadata:
    description: >-
      Enter / XP case — grounded monthly advisor letter. Run the Python engine
      first (python -m engine.facts) to produce build/facts.json, then run this
      graph. Configure the Anthropic API key in Rivet (Settings > Anthropic).
    id: enter_challenge_v2
    title: Enter Challenge (v2 — grounded)
  plugins: []
